  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 148 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nOur week of dry and above normal fall weather will continue through \nthe beginning of the weekend. By Wednesday, a trough moving into the \nIntermountain West will amplify the ridge, which in turn will \nincrease both low level and surface temperatures. As a result, \nThursday is expected to be the warmest day this week with highs in \nthe 70s. Additionally, broad moisture advection will inch dewpoints \nup each day, which in addition to weak winds will mitigate any fire \nweather concerns.\n\nOver the weekend, precipitation chances may return, though there is \nuncertainty in when, where, and to what degree based on model \nspread. Most guidance suggests the wave will not reach the area \nuntil at least Sunday. Due to the high uncertainty, this remains a \nperiod to watch while we enjoy the pleasant fall weather.\n\nLastly, an additional look ahead suggests that while this weekend \nsystem may bring brief near normal temperatures, it will not end our \nstretch of above normal temperatures. CPC highlights a very high \ncombined probabilities (97%) for near normal to above normal \ntemperatures through the end of October, as seen in the 6-10 and 8-\n14 day outlooks.",
